# Exercise 02: Abstract class - Todo List

- [ ] Modify `Animal` class to be abstract
    - [ ] Make `makeSound()` a pure virtual function: `virtual void makeSound() const = 0;`
    - [ ] Rename `Animal` to `AAnimal` (optional but often suggested in the subject for clarity)
- [ ] Ensure `Dog` and `Cat` still work and inherit correctly
- [ ] Create a `main.cpp` to verify abstraction
    - [ ] Attempt to instantiate an `AAnimal` object (should fail at compile time)
    - [ ] Instantiate `Dog` and `Cat` (should work)
    - [ ] Use `AAnimal*` pointers to point to derived objects
- [ ] Verify memory management
- [ ] Ensure Makefile is present and works
